  "Summary": "This bill would require roadway and sidewalk cafe operators to ensure that their outdoor setups are clear of trash, debris, graffiti, vermin, food scraps and unsanitary conditions. Operators who violate this provision would be subject to civil penalties ranging from $200 for the first offense to $500 for the second and subsequent offenses.",
  "TextID": 83438,
  "Text": "Be it enacted by the Council as follows:\n      \n      \n      Section 1. The table of maximum civil penalties in section 19-150 of the administrative code of the city of New York is amended by adding a new row in numerical order to read as follows:\nSection of the Administrative Code\nMaximum Civil Penalty (dollars)\n19-160(b)(6)\n200 (first violation); 500 (second and subsequent violations at the same place of business)\n      � 2. Subdivision b of section 19-160 of the administrative code of the city of New York is amended by adding a new paragraph 6 to read as follows:\n      6. A sidewalk and roadway cafe shall maintain clean setups that are clear of trash, debris, graffiti, vermin, food scraps, and unsanitary conditions. \n      � 3. This local law takes effect 120 days after it becomes law. \n\n\nSS\nLS #22104\n8/5/26 3:00PM\n\n\n      1\n      \n      \n      1",
